    "why": "The exclusion window is opened by a duty in the already-published month and closes inside the horizon: the night of 31 July ends 1 August 08:00 and blocks clinic-cover kinds for ten hours, and the late duty starts at 12:00 on the 1st. The violation is located on the placement INSIDE the horizon, which is the only one a scheduler can act on, and it is the only one this type emits at all -- the anchor duty is not itself wrong, which is why this type reports one placement where overlap_block and min_gap report two. Horizon-local evaluation sees a single duty and reports nothing.",
